From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] wowprospero: trace callers of the faulting guest function

Resolve direct-call targets and dump live entry bytes for the first three
frames in the guest exception chain. This extends the runtime-code trace one
frame above the failing dereference.

diff --git a/wine/wowprospero/cpu.c b/wine/wowprospero/cpu.c
--- a/wine/wowprospero/cpu.c
+++ b/wine/wowprospero/cpu.c
@@ -393,11 +393,11 @@
                          pair[1] - (UINT)sizeof(callsite), callsite[0], callsite[1],
                          callsite[2], callsite[3], callsite[4], callsite[5],
                          callsite[6], callsite[7] );
-                /* When this frame was entered by a direct CALL, resolve the
-                 * target and record its live entry bytes. FalloutNV's return
-                 * site is in a runtime-patched image page, so its static EXE
-                 * disassembly does not describe the code that faulted. */
-                if (i == 0 && pair[1] >= 5)
+                /* For the first three frames, resolve direct CALL targets
+                 * and record their live entry bytes. FalloutNV's frames pass
+                 * through runtime-modified image pages, so static EXE
+                 * disassembly does not describe the code that ran. */
+                if (i < 3 && pair[1] >= 5)
                 {
                     BYTE call[5], target_code[32] = {0};
                     INT displacement;
